Refactor-preserve-tests (Python):

Context: Below is a function used across the codebase with unit tests attached. Perform a surgical refactor to extract a helper, improve readability, and keep behavior identical. Do NOT change function signature or raise new exceptions. Provide only the modified file contents.

--- FILE: utils/transform.py ---
def normalize_items(items):
    # legacy code: sometimes returns duplicates and keeps original order
    out = []
    for x in items:
        if x not in out:
            if isinstance(x, str):
                out.append(x.strip())
            else:
                out.append(x)
    return out

--- TESTS: tests/test_transform.py ---
def test_normalize_items():
    assert normalize_items([" a ", "b", "a"]) == ["a", "b"]

Prompt: "Refactor normalize_items into smaller helpers without changing test outputs. Only return the full file."

Compilation-check refactor (TypeScript):

Context: The function below has nested callbacks and an unnecessary Promise wrapper. Simplify to async/await while preserving public function signature. Return only the updated file content; ensure tsconfig strict mode still compiles.

--- FILE: src/lib/fetcher.ts ---
export function fetchUser(id: string): Promise<User> {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    api.get(`/user/${id}`).then((resp) => {
      if (resp.ok) resolve(resp.body as User);
      else reject(new Error('not found'));
    }).catch(reject);
  });
}

Prompt: "Rewrite fetchUser using async/await and keep the exported signature Promise<User>."
